   "createdAt": "Sat Aug 15 03:14:55 +0000 2026",
   "createdAtLocal": "2026-08-15 11:14",
   "createdAtISO": "2026-08-15T03:14:55+00:00",
   "media": [],
   "urls": [],
   "isRetweet": false,
   "retweetedBy": null,
   "lang": "en",
   "score": null
  },
  {
   "id": "2088547141681807630",
   "text": "64GB will comfortably handle 27B class models even at q6 or q8 weights. You'd only need 128 for 70B+ models or heavy multitasking. Also worth noting, M5 Max has way more memory bandwidth than Pro, which affects tokens/sec more than raw capacity does.\n\na 24GB GPU (like the 3090/4090) paired with a ton of DDR5 RAM could be a strong alternative",
   "author": {
    "id": "2207203190",
    "name": "Alok",
    "screenName": "analogalok",
    "profileImageUrl": "https://pbs.twimg.com/profile_images/2055727708261474304/tUAKpN50_normal.jpg",
