   "id": "2088548501718442466",
   "text": "calling 60 tokens/second \"usable\" is an understatement \n\nBut you're right on the physics. You can't cheat memory bandwidth. We are just getting insanely good at dynamically trading context depth for decode speed depending on exactly what the autonomous loop needs in that moment. 24GB is punching way above its weight class right now.",
